7\n- 07/24/07 auction, 07/31/07 issue: 2-3/8% TIPS—01/15/27 (reopening), price 99.570169\n\nI notice a series of 2-3/8% TIPS with different maturity dates and issue dates within the specified timeframe. These multiple TIPS issues suggest there might be more data points for calculating price volatility than initially considered. I'll need to carefully track each security's price movements between January and August 2007 to compute the standard deviation of their adjusted prices.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_23e8c60bcb4b4e05929edd7f","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport json\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2007_12.json', 'r') as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\n\n# Search for any table with monthly or daily price data for securities\nfor i, el in enumerate(data['document']['elements']):\n    content = el.get('content', '')\n    if content and isinstance(content, str):\n        # Look for \"Table\" with month names or dates\n        if 'Table' in content and ('January' in content or 'February' in content or 'March' in content or \n            'April' in content or 'May' in content or 'June' in content or 'July' in content or 'August' in content):\n            if 'price' in content.lower() or 'yield' in content.lower() or 'TIPS' in content or 'interest' in content.lower():\n                print(f\"Element {i}:\")\n                print(content[:2000])\n                print(\"\\n---\\n\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
